   142	| Duration of illness, mean (SD), y | 4.034 (4.810)  | -              |           |
   143	| Age of onset, mean (SD), y        | 18.341 (7.658) |                |           |
   144	| Y-BOCS score, mean (SD)           | 21.929 (7.137) | -              |           |
   145	| Image quality rating, mean (SD)   | 2.088 (1.875)  | 2.090 (1.850)  | 0.963 b   |
   146	
   147	Note: Y-BOCS: Yale-Brown Obsessive Compulsive Scale; HC, healthy control; OCD, obsessive-compulsive disorder. a Chi-square t -test. b T wo-tailed two sample t test.
   148	
   149	embedded patients with OCD (2 positive and 2 negative weights) into two-dimensional space using t -distributed stochastic neighbor embedding method (hexagrams in Fig. 4C) (Laurens and Hinton 2008).
   150	
   151	## Association between factor compositions and clinical characteristics
   152	
   153	The weights of positive factor 2 (PW2) significantly correlated with illness duration ( r = -0.283, FDR corrected P =0.035) and age of onset ( r = -0.336, FDR corrected P =0.020). The weights of negative factor 1 (NW1) and weights of negative factor 2 (NW2) significantly correlated with the total score of Y-BOCS ( r =0.242, FDR corrected P =0.049 for NW1; r =0.266, FDR corrected P =0.035 for NW2). Female patients exhibited significantly decreased PW2 ( t = -2.303, Cohen' d = -0.466, FDR corrected P =0.047) and increased NW2 ( t =2.319, Cohen' d =0.469, FDR corrected P =0.047) than male patients (Fig. 3).
